e}\le\Box_5$, $D_a$ is then coextensive with $\Diamond_5$. The Barcan formula for $\Box_5$ holds at every type ([[box5-barcan]]), so, transferring it through these actual coextensions, $\Diamond\exists ar x\, .\,\Diamond a\land R[ ar x]	o\exists ar x\, .\,\Diamond(\Diamond a\land R[ ar x])$. This replaces BF in the proof of [[actuality-and-bf-imply-inextensible-comprehension]]: the relation $\lambda ar z\, .\,\Diamond(a\land F[ ar z])$ is coextensive with $F$ and inextensible, since both formulas from which that proof extracts witnesses imply $\Diamond a$.

